WEBVTT

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.930
<i>All right, everyone,</i>
<i>this is the most important part.</i>

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.480
Everything I've said up to now
was just background info

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.480
in order to understand the fate
of this planet.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.110
This moon...

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.450
was following an orbit with our planet,
Ethergeoid, at the center.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.360
Not too close, not too far.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.990
However, eons ago,

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.620
after a meteor shower,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.120
the moon's orbit changed.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.540
And as it continued to orbit,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.500
it gradually began getting closer
to our planet.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.340
No one knows why.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.430
As you may know,
it was discovered that the orbit

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:01.770
will someday get close enough that
the moon will collide with our planet.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.930
This event is inevitable.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.980
It pains me to say it,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.280
but I'm afraid
that I have even more bad news.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.990
When will this moon be
at its closest to our planet?

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.950
I'll give you the answer
that my laboratory calculated.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.630
Approximately 60,000 years in the future.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.800
You guys will be a little older by then.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.100
Professor Henry has a mean streak.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.180
Oh, come on, he's a fun guy.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.880
THE SONG OF ETERNITY

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.550
<i>A song that awakens</i>

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:47.390
<i>And calls</i>

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.520
<i>People repeat the song</i>

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:53.900
<i>In their hearts</i>

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.420
<i>The last song I sung was</i>
<i>the Song of Mortality.</i>

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.600
<i>Instead of dying, my life was spared</i>
<i>and the world was destroyed.</i>

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:33.810
<i>A forbidden song.</i>

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:13.930
<i>I was supposed to die.</i>

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:31.950
<i>Then...</i>

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.080
<i>why...?</i>

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:42.500
<i>And then I understood.</i>

00:05:56.680 --> 00:06:00.480
<i>What it really means to die.</i>

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:09.820
My first impression of her...

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.490
was that she was beautiful.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:19.170
<i>Her skin was very light.</i>
<i>She must have come from a faraway land.</i>

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.690
I was still a child at the time.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:42.190
I wasn't scared or anything.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.650
<i>So, I thought we could be friends.</i>

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:01.080
<i>After a few years went by,</i>
<i>I noticed something strange.</i>

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.340
<i>She didn't look any different.</i>

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:17.470
She hadn't aged one bit
since the day we first met.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.310
You... monster!

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.790
What are you?!

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.580
Stay back!

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:47.880
I don't know what happened after that.
She was soon gone.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:03.690
Finis!

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:07.400
Finis! There you are!

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:12.570
I don't remember when or where...

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.620
she came from anymore.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.370
<i>But there's one thing I can say for sure.</i>

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:24.040
What are you doing?!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:27.710
What did you do?

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.090
-No way.
-Just as I thought.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:36.840
She's a monster!

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.970
<i>That girl will never find happiness.</i>

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:46.560
Witch! She's an immortal witch!

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:51.030
Burn her! Make her burn in hell forever!

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:56.110
I don't know what happened after that.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.530
She was soon gone.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.370
Huh? Finis, right? I know her!

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.330
-We're in the same class.
-Yeah. She's cute.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.050
-Right? I bet she's popular.
-I heard she doesn't have a boyfriend.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.710
Seriously? I didn't expect that.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.220
She doesn't have any friends either.
She's always studying.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.470
She has really good grades
in astronomy, right?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.810
Yeah. She's amazing.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.690
If you think about that,
then we're just...

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.440
-Whoa. What's that?
-It's so loud.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.190
It's so bright.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.730
What is this alarm for?

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:52.710
<i>Having to live forever in a world</i>
<i>without meaning...</i>

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.930
<i>that's what it means to die.</i>

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.780
<i>History repeats itself.</i>

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.860
<i>The same type of world.</i>

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.070
<i>The same type of people.</i>

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.080
<i>No matter how much progress</i>
<i>civilization makes,</i>

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.460
<i>everything always gets reset</i>
<i>for one reason or another.</i>

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:34.000
<i>It will repeat itself, over and over.</i>

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:45.930
Henry...

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.020
Even though I'm an astronomer,

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.770
there are many things I don't know.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:55.360
That's why your stories are
so interesting.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.820
You have so much knowledge.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:02.490
The natural sciences, the humanities
and the formal sciences...

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.950
There's no one like you
in the modern age.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.000
The modern age?

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.960
What is the modern age?

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:16.090
Is this a quiz?

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.550
There is no such thing as the modern age.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:20.630
The past
and the future don't exist either.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:23.680
The past is the future,
and the future is the past.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.060
Are you talking about physics?
Or about philosophy?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:31.190
Trying to define time is something
that humans do to satisfy their egos,

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:33.980
but I'm sad to hear you say
that there is no future.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.360
There is no beginning,
and there is no end.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.280
If you head towards the end,
you will reach the beginning.

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:42.450
Everything is a circle.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.700
So, you must not hold on to hope.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:50.040
I used to have hope.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.040
<i>If the world repeats itself,</i>

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:58.170
<i>maybe I could return</i>
<i>to that exact same instance one day.</i>

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.430
<i>Not to an age that looks similar,</i>
<i>but is actually different.</i>

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:07.680
<i>I just have to continue to wait forever</i>
<i>until I arrive in an age...</i>

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.600
<i>that's exactly the same</i>
<i>as the one I was born in.</i>

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.440
You... monster!

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:17.900
<i>No matter how many times</i>
<i>I've suffered from hatred,</i>

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:22.280
<i>I just have to keep waiting</i>
<i>until I meet the exact same person.</i>

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:25.910
<i>That's what I used to think.</i>

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.130
Sorry.

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:41.130
Um...

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:48.180
-Hen--
-Henry! What's wrong?

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:49.970
Oh, it's nothing.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.020
If you don't hurry, you'll be late
for the recital.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:54.600
-Yup.
-Dad, hurry up!

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:55.520
Okay.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.190
<i>I was wrong.</i>

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:06.200
<i>No matter how similar,</i>

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.990
<i>there's no way</i>
<i>their hearts could be the same.</i>

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.450
<i>The Henry that I loved...</i>

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.120
<i>will never come back.</i>

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.550
The Henry that I killed...

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.180
will never come back.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.390
The Star Song Festival, huh?

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.730
They say it's a festival
for singing to the stars,

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.310
but it's really a festival

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:39.310
where if you sing to the stars,
your wishes come true.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.780
Kids these days forget about traditions.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:45.650
What was it called?
The Song of Spirits, right?

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:48.410
The orchestra is going to sing it
at the festival, right?

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:51.700
-But not at the summer festival, right?
-Are you going this year?

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:55.370
The Star Song Festival is the day
on which the stars are the closest.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:57.870
All the villagers will perform together.

00:13:59.630 --> 00:14:02.090
<i>As history repeats itself forever,</i>

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.300
<i>in every age and in every civilization,</i>

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:09.010
<i>I made them continue telling the legend</i>
<i>of the Star Song Festival</i>

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:10.760
<i>and the Ancient Songstress.</i>

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.140
<i>Since I can intervene in any era</i>
<i>and any place,</i>

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:18.100
<i>then I should create a legend.</i>

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:24.020
<i>I should make the history</i>
<i>of this world itself a part of my plan.</i>

00:14:25.110 --> 00:14:28.030
I like the legend
of the Ancient Songstress.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:30.780
Book sales go up around the time
of the festival, too.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:35.040
She ended a war with her songs.
She's a strong woman who I look up to.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.830
But when did this legend start?

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.080
No one knows the author, right?

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:45.250
<i>What I need to do is to create a backdrop</i>
<i>for people</i>

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:52.260
<i>There's just one reason.</i>

00:14:53.510 --> 00:14:56.390
<i>To sing that song... one more time.</i>

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:00.730
<i>I kept deceiving the world...</i>

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:06.070
<i>until the moment when the stars were</i>
<i>at their closest again.</i>

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:16.410
Finis!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:22.670
Are you saying that you're
the Ancient Songstress?

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.130
There's no way that could be true!

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:28.710
What are you trying to do?!

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:34.640
The power of songs is amplified
when there are melodies,

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.680
rhythms and harmonies.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:39.100
It becomes stronger than singing alone.

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.440
I was singing alone at that time.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.230
That's why I was only able
to summon meteors.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.490
That's why this time...

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:52.400
You summoned meteors with a song?

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:54.620
Songs are sound waves!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.200
It couldn't be transmitted through space--

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.870
"Even though I'm an astronomer,
there are many things I don't know."

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.580
That's what you said.

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:13.630
The power of songs created
from limited scales and lyrics...

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.140
acts on dark matter and dark energy.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:21.930
The reason that the moon's orbit changed
in ancient times...

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:23.600
is due to my song.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.060
I'm grateful to you.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:30.530
The orbit of that moon is
the only thing I didn't know.

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:35.030
Now that I know it, I can execute my plan.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.070
Your plan?

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:41.330
When the stars are at their closest,
I will sing.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.250
I will sing with music again.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:48.500
The Song of Mortality.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:53.630
Don't worry, Henry.

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:59.760
You'll be gone by then.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:12.030
<i>It's only a matter of time before a war</i>
<i>breaks out with neighboring Granadia.</i>

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:16.610
I cannot keep appointing you to be
the general, now that you're getting old.

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.990
I understand.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:25.080
Without you,
our country would not have prospered.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:27.500
Everyone, sing his praises!

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:30.290
You shall go down in history,

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.920
General Talgia Hawkray!

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:37.180
General Talgia Hawkray!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:42.100
Ever since we got a new general,
we've been on a winning streak.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.640
But I heard he leaves nothing
but burned ruins behind

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.850
and scares the enemy.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:50.190
If Hawkray hadn't retired,
this wouldn't have happened.

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:53.530
The general is passing through! Make way!

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:59.620
So, that's General Bazra Bearmors.

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:03.830
We started winning
after that shady-looking person joined.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.330
I wonder who it is.

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:11.630
It's them! It's Bazra's unit
from the Kingdom of Golt!

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:54.170
<i>Was it by chance, or was it destiny?</i>

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:59.300
<i>As history repeated itself again,</i>
<i>the end that I had been waiting for...</i>

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:02.470
<i>was the exact same age as back then.</i>

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:05.850
<i>It was convenient for me that way.</i>

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:21.230
<i>It's been a long time, Hawkray!</i>

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:29.200
<i>Into the sky from which</i>
<i>The light has disappeared</i>

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.950
What do I shine there?

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:38.210
I see you're in excellent spirits.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:00.770
It's just a little longer
until the Star Song Festival.

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:08.820
Hey. Over there!

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:13.700
Could it be...?

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:16.080
Is that Finis?
